  "confirmed_adjacent_fix": {
    "after": "Defer successor announcement while sendItems is empty. The ordinary current-contract head resumes first and recovers its full verified proof. A second application Pack admitted while that head is outstanding still announces and acknowledges the successor exactly once.",
    "before": "Non-head successor announcement became first outstanding Pack. Its resend was promoted to a head carrying the successor proof while contract_ahead kept that successor non-current. The receiver lacked the authenticated current contract and rejected it with No contract; sender exhausted its lifetime.",
    "controls": [
      "plain and encrypted idle resume",
      "combined receiver sequence and cipher loss",
      "single missing-contract response loss recovery",
      "permanent feedback loss retains ACK and gap timeout evidence",
      "normal successor prefetch and exactly-once payload after head",
      "wrong-contract request rejection",
      "foreign/malformed encryption generation rejection",
      "malformed signed-contract rejection",
      "owner cancellation and pool ownership"
    ],
    "performance_boundary": "Sparse or NoAck-only traffic can defer an ahead announcement until an acknowledged current-contract Pack is outstanding; queued grants and byte/deadline thresholds remain unchanged.",
    "production_change": "One len(sendItems)==0 guard plus explanatory comment; no receiver authentication, proof contents, protocol, budgets, deadline or acceptance threshold changed.",
    "production_files": [
      "transfer.go"
    ],
    "r46_attribution": "Adjacent proven defect only. All18 exact R46 peer windows lack the reproduced no-contract/contract-verification error witness, so this fix is not claimed to resolve their root cause.",
    "test_layer": "Real SendBuffer/ReceiveBuffer workers, production protobuf codecs, standard SHA256 HMAC verified signed grants, generated test identities, actual TLS sessions, in-memory route wires, testing/synctest fake clock, locked generation snapshots and joined workers.",
    "trigger": "Receiver retires after155 seconds of idle; unchanged sender remains. A fresh prefetched successor is available and the resumed application crosses the unchanged lead floor."
  },
  "go_version": "go version go1.26.6 linux/amd64",
  "live_fleet_modified": false,
  "main_checkout_modified": false,
  "next_reproduction_requirements": [
    "Bounded per-sequence progress keyed by sequence ID and message ID: head flag, sequence number, contract-ahead flag, compact/full proof kind, verified contract ID, encryption role/epoch and exact route generation.",
    "Missing-contract request generation, ACK write start/end disposition, peer ACK decode/admission and full-contract resend disposition with monotonic times and bounded counts.",
    "Receiver generation create/idle retirement, cipher availability and first unresolved queue item. Keep sender ACK lifetime and receiver gap timeout strict.",
    "For each failed health probe: deadline, start/end, transport error class or HTTP status, bounded sanitized response and omission counters.",
    "For each unhealthy swarm: configured/running/disabled counts and distinct connection-vs-registration readiness transitions, correlated with exact fault apply/restore time and block.",
    "For an unhealthy RPC proxy: bind supervisor HTTP result to upstream dial start/end and error class; do not increase deadlines merely to hide a failed probe.",
    "Use existing -tags acklineagetrace with a non-nil bounded nonblocking ProgressObserver for a diagnostic reproduction; the tag alone records nothing. A source search of pinned SN miner/validator and SDK device_local* found no ProgressObserver or TransferWireMessageObserver installation.",
    "Preserve exact synthetic155-second receiver-retirement barrier and retained sender; vary a single feedback boundary at a time on the actual reliable carrier: receiver request creation, local ACK-route write refusal, carrier handoff, sender decode/admission. One lost response must recover; permanent loss must retain strict failures.",
    "Do not treat the fixed prefetched-successor boundary as the18-event cause without a matching per-message witness."
  ],
